<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia coffee group to debate internal price.</title>
<headline>Colombia coffee group to debate internal price.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's National Coffee Growers' Federation is set to consider proposals to revise the internal price paid to growers at a meeting Tuesday night, Finance Minister Jose Antonio Ocampo said.</p>
<p>The current price for a 125-kg load was frozen until further notice at 431,375 pesos at a meeting Friday.</p>
<p>The federation originally agreed in January to begin calculating payments on a sliding-scale formula to track the sharp run-up in international prices. The system was to remain in effect until prices reached $2.60 per lb in international markets but last week the price rose above $3 for the first time in 20 years before dropping back.</p>
</text>
